****************************************************************  8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
Resolved Resonance Region Evaluation: 1e-11 to 1.5 MeV            8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
   P. Brain*, Y.Danon*, D.Brown", A. Lewis^, and D. Barry^        8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
  *Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute                               8237 1451
     Troy, NY 12180, USA brainp@rpi.edu                           8237 1451
  "Brookhaven National Laboratory                                 8237 1451
     Upton, NY 11973-5000, USA                                    8237 1451
  ^Naval Nuclear Laboratory                                       8237 1451
     Schenectady, New York 12301-1072, USA                        8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
****************************************************************  8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 The resolved resonance evaluation utilized transmission and      8237 1451
 capture data sets [ref01-06] in the SAMMY code [ref07].          8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 Base resonance parameters taken from ENDF/B-VIII [ref08].        8237 1451
 The effective scattering radius R' was changed to 9.75 fm to     8237 1451
 get proper potential scattering term [ref09].                    8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 Constraining the capture cross section was done with Maxwellian  8237 1451
 Averaged Cross Sections (MACS) at 30 keV. Work by Beer, Allen    8237 1451
 [ref10], Weissman [ref11] demonstrated that MACS(30 keV) should  8237 1451
 be 0.35 mb. Due to the poor capture data on this isotope, many   8237 1451
 resonance have an average radiation width which was changed to   8237 1451
 get the above MACS(30 keV). In addition, a direct capture        8237 1451
 component was added in MF-3. Capture cross section around 10 eV  8237 1451
 is now 10x greater than ENDF/B-VIII but the average resonance    8237 1451
 contribution is down by a factor of 2.                           8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 The resolved resonance was extended from 1 MeV to 1.5 MeV using  8237 1451
 Carlton transmission data [ref04] and RPI scattering             8237 1451
 measurements with nautral lead [ref12]. Due to spin              8237 1451
 insensitivity of certain transmission energies, a regressive     8237 1451
 method of spin assignments was developed using SAMMY,            8237 1451
 NJOY [ref13], and MCNP [ref14]. Cross section integral           8237 1451
 comparisons were made between R-matrix and pointwise cross       8237 1451
 sections to ensure no more than 1% in integral cross section     8237 1451
 was changed as a result of formalism change.                     8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 -------------------------------------------------------------    8237 1451
 Cross Section(2200 m/s)   RPI (b)             NIST (b)           8237 1451
 total                     11.50            11.34 +/- 0.15        8237 1451
 elastic                   11.50            11.34 +/- 0.15        8237 1451
 capture                 0.000235         0.00023 +/- 0.00002     8237 1451
 -------------------------------------------------------------    8237 1451
 Resonance Integral              RPI (b)                          8237 1451
 total                      1.39846E+02                           8237 1451
 elastic                    1.39845E+02                           8237 1451
 capture                    7.87194E-04                           8237 1451
 -------------------------------------------------------------    8237 1451
 Scattering Length         RPI(fm)            NIST (fm)           8237 1451
 bound coherent            9.55             9.50 +/- 0.06         8237 1451
 -------------------------------------------------------------    8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 MF-4 was recalculated from resonance parameters on a high        8237 1451
 resolution energy grid within the RRR limits using NJOY16[ref13] 8237 1451
 with Blatt-Biedenharn formalism enabed.                          8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 MF-32 was produced with SAMMY.                                   8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 MF-34 was produced with SAMMY and Python using correlated        8237 1451
 sampling of MF-32 to create synthetic MF-2 and MF-4.             8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 MF-33 calculated with CoH and KALMAN filter, specifically        8237 1451
 MT-1,2,4,16,102.                                                 8237 1451
****************************************************************  8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
Fast Region Evaluation: 1.5 to 20 MeV                             8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
   T.Kawano&, P. Brain*, Y.Danon*, D.Brown", and D. Barry^        8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
  *Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute                               8237 1451
     Troy, NY 12180, USA brainp@rpi.edu                           8237 1451
  &Los Alamos National Laboratory                                 8237 1451
     Los Alamos,New Mexico 87545, USA                             8237 1451
  "Brookhaven National Laboratory                                 8237 1451
     Upton, NY 11973-5000, USA                                    8237 1451
  ^Naval Nuclear Laboratory                                       8237 1451
     Schenectady, New York 12301-1072, USA                        8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
****************************************************************  8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
 Full calculation of all reaction channels from threshold to 20   8237 1451
 MeV using CoH-3 [ref15] Hauser Feschbach Statistical Code.       8237 1451
 Kunieda global fit OMP parameters adjusted to fit experimental   8237 1451
 data [ref03] [ref16]. Coupled channels and DWBA used for         8237 1451
 inelastic channels with a vibrational deformation model.         8237 1451
 Resonance structure that could not be resolved but is present    8237 1451
 in transmission data sets were included to elastic and inelastic 8237 1451
 partial channels such that the total calculated cross section    8237 1451
 matches the experimental. Angular distributions for all          8237 1451
 reactions were calculated from CoH-3.                            8237 1451
                                                                  8237 1451
